What a native renderer needs from the runtime. PS2Memory::setDmaStartObserver: a callback when the guest starts a VIF1 or GIF DMA transfer (channel, CHCR, MADR, QWC, TADR), before the runtime takes it up, so a renderer can read the same chain from RDRAM in the order the guest sends it. GSFrontend::getContext: a drawing context's registers as the GS has them (an HLE double-buffer setup writes the drawing environment outside the guest's DMA transfers). The host's replacement hook also gets the emulated frame (always uploaded now) and the part present() shows, so a renderer can show its picture beside the emulated one. PS2X_WINDOW_SIZE=WxH opens the window at that size. PS2Memory::saveEeTimers/restoreEeTimers save and put back the four EE timers (a test harness replays each recorded call from the same timer state). Checked in Metropolismania: the native renderer draws the title, menus, text, HUD, minimap and movies from these hooks beside the emulated picture; difftest replays exact with the timers restored.

